{
 "_provenance": "Recorded 2026-11-04 on plexscratch42 (Plex Media Server 1.42.2.10156-f737b826c, unclaimed, offline) from two sections made for it: `videoext-movies` (Plex Movie scanner, tv.plex.agents.movie) and `videoext-shows` (Plex TV Series scanner, tv.plex.agents.series). One small file per extension of the legacy scanner's video_exts (fun's Scanners.bundle VideoFiles.py), plus .mk3d, .ifo, .iso and a DVD VIDEO_TS folder: written by ffmpeg 4.4.2 on the lab host wherever it has a muxer (a DVD by dvdauthor 0.7.2 and genisoimage), else a real file from samples.ffmpeg.org (fli, nsv, nuv, pva, ty, viv, vp3, svq3, rmvb, ogm, avs, dvr-ms), and text for the playlists. Per extension: whether the scan made a Part of it, its Media's container and stream count, the part read's status and Content-Type for `Range: bytes=0-9` (`location` where it redirected), and over the 78 client profiles' plain-form http decisions how many direct play, convert, answer neither or 400 (tests/fixtures/decisions/ holds the cells). `media` names the tests/fixtures/media/ fixture holding the file's probe and Media. `mk3d.probe` is ffprobe 4.4.2's probe of a real .mk3d, a 44 GB 3D Blu-ray remux served by a production zurg over localhost (its file name replaced): what a source pushes for one.",
